{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501490-mystery-enlightenment-what-or-when","id":501490,"title":"Mystery Enlightenment - What, or when?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-03T01:26:42-07:00","id":501490,"title":"Mystery Enlightenment - What, or when?","content":"So, I'm curious about something. I've found a paragraph in the segment about the mysteries of the dragon in V:tR 2e core (pg. 155) Specifically, it refers to, 'Enlightenment' existing at the pinnacle of each coil. What exactly would this look like? Is it something high-end that would totally change how the game is played like Equinox Road's, 'Game of immortals' or Imperial Mysteries? Or is it something you're never meant to learn outside of the focus of an entire chronicle, like Golconda or the general idea of transcendence? If the devs could answer that'd be awesome, but I'd sooner expect others to give their two cents. What're your thoughts on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T11:23:27-07:00","id":503172,"title":"","content":"I'm quite interested in this as well, seeing as my Ordo Dracul Gangrel is going to go all the way through the the Mystery of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> As for how they become &quot;enlightened&quot; I suppose it depends on the mystery. Wyrm could be a bit of a fusion of man and beast, while also remaining disciplined. Voivode could be of a more kingly or regal aura around the vampire as well as acting as such (Think Griffith from Berserk if you're into that). Ascendant could potentially make the vampire seem all the more human in comparison to other vampires. I'm not totally sure on all of these, but they seem to be good fits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3183-shomaxt","name":"Shomaxt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T15:28:01-07:00","id":503558,"title":"","content":"That'd be the fifth-dot power and a greater sense of entitlement that your view of the Vampiric condition is &quot;correct&quot; because see what all that view has achieved for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T12:25:04-07:00","id":504489,"title":"","content":"A Coil's enlightenment/sixth dot is explicitly stated to ideally change you into not a kindred, at least in the sense that you were sired. In my view it would take the previous powers and use their theme to change something about the rules of vampirism, such as:<br /> <br /> <b>Ascendent:</b> you always have the blush of live active, and can spend blood points at the beginning of the night for the purposes of Sun's Forgotten Kiss, or you can spend a point of blood to negate the effects of banes for the scene, or so on.<br /> <b>Wyrm:</b> you no longer have any problems directing your frenzy, or can apply the bonus from frenzy to any type of roll, or the like.<br /> <b>Voivode:</b> you now have blood sympathy with your entire clan, can embrace vampires of other clans, or something.<br /> <br /> However, if it's ever reached, enlightenment will also likely be very personal for a vampire and different to the experiences of others who reached it. One might loose kindred powers as they move further away, whereas another might strengthen the power of his disciplines, and a third might develop Strix-like powers (better keep those secret).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T16:05:05-07:00","id":509285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501490-mystery-enlightenment-what-or-when?p=504489#post504489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wyrm:</b> you no longer have any problems directing your frenzy, or can apply the bonus from frenzy to any type of roll, or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that a true master of the Mystery of the Wyrm would have completely merged his beast with his rational mind, gaining all of the benefits of his coils while retaining a degree of control similar to what he has when not in frenzy.<br /> <br /> &quot;That's my secret, neonate. I'm <i>always</i> angry.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T04:04:33-07:00","id":509771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501490-mystery-enlightenment-what-or-when?p=509285#post509285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine that a true master of the Mystery of the Wyrm would have completely merged his beast with his rational mind, gaining all of the benefits of his coils while retaining a degree of control similar to what he has when not in frenzy.<br /> <br /> 'That's my secret, neonate. I'm <i>always</i> angry.'</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I meant by no problems, maybe he wants to direct his frenzy to having a nice <s>cup of tea and</s> chat with the prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user"